i know who you are  you know who you are  just say it  come on  hey guys pete here over the last couple  of days there's been a lot of discussion  about the back-to-back trailers better  call saul just put out for the final  episodes we're just a little more than  one week away from the premiere of  episode 8 and there's some potential  good news and some potential bad news in  this pair of teasers the good news is  that we got what appears to be our first  look at actual new footage from the  final episodes and the bad news is that  it looks like they had to recast the  character jeff who was originally played  by the actor don harvey that's what i'm  here to talk about and if any of that  sounds like spoilers or you're averse to  speculation then this video won't be for  you and with that out of the way let's  get into it we got a couple of teasers  over the last two days and the first one  which is called gene's world created  quite the stir in that we see mostly  recycled footage of gene takavic in  omaha there are shots of him working at  cinnabon and making himself a rusty nail  cocktail at home from the very first  episode from season 5 there's a shot of  him looking paranoid peeking out his  window one of him pouring out the  diamonds he has hidden in a band-aid tin  on his table and him on the phone  telling ed to disappear that he got made  before he says i'm going to fix it  myself which is of course how they ended  the last scene that we've seen of him  from season 4 there's a shot of him in  the backseat of jeff's cab followed by  one of him looking scared after he gets  out all of this old footage is there to  remind us of gene's situation his frame  of mind and what he was up to when we  last saw him there's not much that  stands out in that except maybe showing  the diamonds ties in with the idea of  him paying jeff off which the last  teaser seemed to hint at they did choose  to show two shots of him peeking out of  the window from different seasons but  one's interior and one's exterior so  they naturally go together and to me  that just reinforces that he's  constantly looking over his shoulder the  new footage is an overhead shot of  someone eating a cinnabon with a knife  and fork and it's a mystery as to who  this is because they're wearing a  wedding ring we know jimmy never wore  one and in the scenes where don harvey  played jeff he isn't wearing one either  the big thing in this trailer that got  everyone talking was that even though  it's cut together with saul sitting in  the back seat the shots of jeff's cab  now have a different actor sitting in  the driver's seat in a much brighter  looking scene the voice also sounds a  little bit off when he says it's you it  is you right away people started  guessing that they recast the actor my  initial thought was that gene had called  up the taxi company like jeff told him  to in the mall scene and someone else  had to come pick him up in his car i  knew dawn harvey was in we own the city  which just wrapped up on hbo and figured  that they probably were filmed at the  same time i built an elaborate theory  that included schedule changes because  of bob's heart attack and coveted  restrictions that would make gene  meeting someone else in jeff's circle  necessary but i did assume that the  original actor would still be involved  in some way primarily because i think  that gene going after jeff is going to  be a big part of how the series comes to  an end and these two new teasers do kind  of reinforce that idea  not long after i put my super theory  together it took a couple of quick hits  first the fan account all about saul  posted that they had inside information  that jeff had been recast then the  second teaser came out where the new  actor is wearing the same sweater that  jeff had on in the season 5 mall scene i  was able to imagine someone else driving  his car but them doing that while  wearing his sweater doesn't work nearly  as well i will come back to the details  about the recast but first i want to  talk about the second teaser that opens  with the albuquerque isotopes air  freshener dangling from the rear view  mirror of jeff's cab the camera switches  from that to focus on the driver looking  back just like it did when the character  was first introduced when he picked up  gene at the hospital after he collapsed  in the kitchen at cinnabon in this  version you see that this is a  completely unrelated shot of him driving  during the day they name this one you  know who you are and you hear some of  the dialogue from when they first talked  remember he was pressuring him into  admitting that he was saul goodman from  the commercials he used to always see  when he lived in albuquerque here you  can tell without question that this is  not don harvey's voice as i mentioned  this is during the day so this is brand  new footage with a brand new actor with  some dialogue that's been re-recorded in  his voice that all seems to be in line  with recasting the character i suppose  that hearing these lines in his voice  led some people to think that they  re-shot the scenes with jeff completely  but i don't think that really makes  sense also in all about saul's post they  said that the reshoot in the cab was an  introduction to the new jeff so that we  can be prepared to see that when it airs  and hopefully not be so jarring  initially that sounded like they redid  those scenes but after seeing the second  bit of footage that happens at a  different time and place it seems more  likely that they just added the new  actor's voice to signal the change the  reason for the recast seems to be  schedule conflicts based on don harvey's  role in we own the city while jeff is an  important character for better call saul  he's not part of the main cast i'm not  entirely sure how those things work but  it doesn't seem like they would be able  to keep him on contract between seasons  it is disappointing because he did such  a good job in the short amount of time  he had on screen but these things happen  pretty often if you think about shows  that run for multiple seasons over a  number of years ultimately it's not that  important in my eyes and probably won't  make that big of a difference in the big  picture they cast the role the first  time and that turned out great why  wouldn't they be able to do a competent  job of replacing him the weird part is  that these trailers really stirred up a  lot of fans and there was no official  announcement that they were bringing a  new actor in i've seen several fan  reports that say the new actor is pat  healy which seemed like a credible  enough idea it definitely looks like him  and he's been engaging with a lot of  better call saul stuff on his social  media but it seems like it would be  pretty easy for the show to pass this  information onto a news outlet and get  it out there if they wanted to temper  expectations around don harvey's return  at this time there's been no official  announcement in the press or on social  media and people are definitely trying  to get them to say something for now i  guess it's nice to see some brand new  footage that adds to all the speculation  they've been stirring up with the promos  they already put out and it does look  like the recast is probably happening as  far as the instagram account that i  mentioned that claimed to have the  insider information about it all about  saul is an account i'm familiar with i  don't know them but i would describe  them as an earnest fan who lives in  albuquerque and posts useful information  because they love the show i don't  really see an angle to making something  like this up but it's possible that  their source doesn't have complete or  correct information it won't be long  until we see it with our own eyes i do  wonder who is eating the cinnabon in  that first clip and i think that's a  good place to leave things let me know  in the comments what you think about the  new teasers the unfortunate recasting  and how jeff will play into the end game  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already and thanks for watching  i'll talk to you soon

